<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6653" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cappădŏcĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππαδοκία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a country of Asia Minor</i>, <i>north
				of Cilicia</i>, <i>between the Taurus and
			Pontus</i>, now called <i>Caramania</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 3,
				3, § 8 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr.
				2, 21, 55</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 5, 18, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
				15, 2, 1 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 3, 1, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Eum. 2,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cappădox</span></b> ,
				ŏcis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππάδοξ</span>, <i>a
			Cappaaocian</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Red. in Sen. 6,
			14</span></i>.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 2,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 8, 5</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin. 6,
				3, 3, § 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 6,
				39</span></i>; Gr. acc. Cappadŏcas, <i><span class="en">Pers. 6,
			77</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">appos. equi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. 4, 6, 3</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cappădŏcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Cappadocia</i>, <i>Cappadocian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					10, 184</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 2, 2, § 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">catastae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					10, 76</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Pers. 6, 77</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					6, 17, 7</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 31, 7, 39, § 73 sq.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lactuca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					10, 191</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 10, 184</span></i>; also <i>absol.</i> Cappadoca, <i><span class="en">Mart. 5, 78</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cappădŏcĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Cappadocian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lactuca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 3, 26</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">the preced.: zizipha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 9, 27, § 51</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			CAPPADOCICVSEXERCITVS, upon a coin of Adrian, in Eckh. Doct. Num. 6,
			p. 493.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cap-pădŏcarchĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καππαδοκαρχια</span>, <i>the priest</i>'<i>s office in Cappadocia</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 27, 1,
				6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
